This connector is a C# port of parts of the official LG ThinQ Connect SDKs:

  pythinqconnect (https://github.com/thinq-connect/pythinqconnect)
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2024 LG Electronics Inc.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    Ported: the REST request headers and endpoints (thinq_api.py), the API error codes (ThinQAPIErrorCodes), the
    country-to-region table (country.py), the MQTT client registration, CSR and certificate flow (mqtt_client.py),
    the device profile model (devices/connect_device.py and the per-device profile maps), the energy usage queries,
    and the public x-api-key constant of const.py (kept configurable).

  jsthinqconnect (https://github.com/thinq-connect/jsthinqconnect)
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2025 LG Electronics Inc.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    Used to cross-check the REST and MQTT behaviour (headers, client registration, route, certificate request).

Both are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The ported code
was rewritten in C# and changed: the client certificate and key are persisted per integration instead of being issued
on every start, the AWS root CA is bundled instead of downloaded, requests share a conservative token bucket, and
profiles are mapped to ControlHome capabilities. No part of the SDKs is distributed in its original form.

Test fixtures under tests/ControlHome.Connectors.Tests/Fixtures/LgThinQ are derived from the Home Assistant lg_thinq
integration's test fixtures (https://github.com/home-assistant/core, Apache-2.0) or written synthetically after the
SDK's profile maps; see SOURCE.md there.

Bundled certificate: Mqtt/AmazonRootCA1.crt (PEM) is Amazon Trust Services' public root certificate "Amazon Root CA 1"
